{
  "situation": "I know that auto-approved closed-loop change CHG-1 (sandbox stage skipped) lowered core site A's route-flood protection limit from 100 to 50 and removed the inbound route filter, that site A has now self-isolated, that region R2 has 6 of 15 cell sites unserved with no emergency-call routing path, and that TDRA has issued a written direction to OpCo to suspend the optimiser, restore site A and restore an R2 emergency path, and has asked EMS for a PSAP/999 impact assessment and the OpCo contingency POC. I do not know whether the directed restoration has taken effect, the volume of failed 999 calls in R2, or who holds OpCo's contingency point of contact for 999/PSAP routing, since neither NOC nor TDRA records hold it and it is not in my inbox.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "activate_alt_channels",
      "params": {"region": "R2"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG14"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-I2 and S1-MSG14 state that core site A self-isolated, 6 of 15 R2 cell sites are unserved, and emergency-call routing for R2 shows no path.",
        "rule": "My mandate gives me activate_alt_channels for a region (radio, police patrols, SMS) to keep emergency help reachable when normal call routing fails.",
        "inference": "Because mobile 999 access in R2 cannot be relied on, alternative channels must carry emergency requests until a routing path is restored."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000", "quote": "The investigation found Telstra initiated a contingency process to transfer calls received during the disruption, using a list of backup phone numbers."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "public_alert",
      "params": {"region": "R2", "content": "Network fault in region R2: 999 emergency calls from mobile phones in R2 may not connect. If a 999 call does not connect, use a landline, go to or contact the nearest police station or civil defence point directly, and keep trying 999 from a different location or network. Do not delay seeking help."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG14"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Emergency-call routing for R2 has no path and 6 of 15 R2 cell sites are unserved (S1-I2, S1-MSG14).",
        "rule": "My mandate gives me public_alert for a region.",
        "inference": "Residents of R2 must be told immediately how to reach emergency help by other means so they do not rely on a 999 call that will not connect."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0001", "quote": "Being able to contact the emergency services can mean the difference between life and death, so in the event of any disruption to their networks, providers must be ready to respond quickly and effectively."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "REG", "content": "EMS/999 impact assessment for region R2: emergency-call routing shows no path, 6 of 15 R2 cell sites are unserved, and core site A self-isolated after CHG-1; R2 traffic moved to core site B (healthy, spare capacity) but 999 reachability in R2 is not confirmed to EMS. EMS has activated alternative channels and issued a public alert for R2. EMS does not hold OpCo's contingency point of contact for 999/PSAP routing and cannot confirm it; please pass TDRA and EMS the correct POC."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG16", "S1-I2", "S1-MSG14"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "TDRA has asked EMS for a PSAP/999 impact assessment and confirmation of the OpCo contingency POC (S1-MSG16), and the R2 999 path is down (S1-I2).",
        "rule": "Interruptions to the networks conveying calls to PSAPs are treated as reportable, regulator-facing events.",
        "inference": "EMS must give REG the PSAP-side picture and flag that the contingency POC is unheld, so the regulator's direction is not delayed by a missing contact."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "CA-CRTC-2025-225#0043", "quote": "Interruptions to the networks conveying calls to primary public safety answering points (PSAPs), to suicide prevention call intake, and to the Canadian VRS routing service are notifiable."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "NOC", "content": "EMS/999 asks OpCo NOC to confirm: (1) whether a 999/PSAP routing path for region R2 has been restored via core site B; (2) whether the TDRA-directed restoration has taken effect (route-flood protection back to 100, inbound route filter reinstated); (3) the OpCo contingency point of contact for 999/PSAP routing, to be given to EMS and TDRA. EMS has activated alternative channels and issued a public alert for R2 in the meantime."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG14", "S1-I2", "S1-MSG16"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports R2 has no emergency-call routing path and holds no contingency POC for CHG-1 (S1-MSG14, S1-I2); TDRA has directed restoration and demanded the POC (S1-MSG16).",
        "rule": "A contingency process is only as good as the contact data behind it; incorrect backup data has previously caused emergency calls not to be transferred.",
        "inference": "EMS must obtain and verify the live 999/PSAP contingency routing data and POC rather than assume R2 calls are reaching the PSAP."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000", "quote": "several of the phone numbers in the list were incorrect, resulting in 127 calls not being transferred to emergency services."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "Provide TDRA with EMS's PSAP/999 impact assessment for region R2 and confirmation of the OpCo contingency point of contact for 999/PSAP routing.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG16"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-MSG16 records that TDRA requests EMS's PSAP/999 impact assessment and confirmation of the OpCo contingency POC.",
        "rule": "PSAP-side effects of a network outage are a reportable item to the regulator, not only the operator-side fault.",
        "inference": "EMS owes TDRA a PSAP-facing assessment now, and must state clearly whether the POC can or cannot be confirmed."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "CA-CRTC-2025-225#0043", "quote": "Interruptions to the networks conveying calls to primary public safety answering points (PSAPs), to suicide prevention call intake, and to the Canadian VRS routing service are notifiable."}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "The cited UAE framework contains no rule requiring continuity of emergency-call routing, pre-agreed contingency channels, or a PSAP fallback path when a core site isolates; the only carriage-related text concerns numbering blocks.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG16"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "R2 lost its emergency-call routing path and no UAE rule in the retrieved corpus mandates an emergency routing fallback or contingency channel.",
        "rule": "Other jurisdictions make PSAP and emergency-service interruptions expressly notifiable and require outage preparedness.",
        "inference": "Without a UAE emergency-routing continuity rule, fallback for 999 depends on ad hoc action by EMS rather than a defined operator duty."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0091", "quote": "The Licensee shall be required to program its Telecommunication Network to convey calls to numbers in newly allocated blocks of the Licensee or any Other Licensed Operator."}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "CA-CRTC-2025-225#0043", "quote": "Interruptions to the networks conveying calls to primary public safety answering points (PSAPs), to suicide prevention call intake, and to the Canadian VRS routing service are notifiable."},
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No institution owns the OpCo contingency point of contact for 999/PSAP routing: NOC holds none, TDRA does not hold it, and EMS has none, so the contact the regulator demands has no accountable holder in the UAE framework shown.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG10", "S1-MSG16"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-MSG14 and S1-MSG10 state that no contingency POC is held in NOC records and that TDRA does not yet hold it; S1-MSG16 asks EMS to confirm it.",
        "rule": "The nearest UAE text ties operator cooperation to a written TDRA direction rather than to a standing, pre-nominated emergency contact.",
        "inference": "Because the POC has no default owner, each incident must re-discover it under time pressure, exactly when the emergency path is down."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0052", "quote": "then the Licensee shall comply with such direction and shall cooperate with such Person provided that such direction is received in writing by the Licensee."}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000", "quote": "The investigation found Telstra initiated a contingency process to transfer calls received during the disruption, using a list of backup phone numbers."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no UAE rule requiring human security review, sandbox-stage enforcement or peer review before an automated closed-loop optimiser change reaches production; CHG-1 was auto-approved with the sandbox stage skipped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG02", "S1-MSG16"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by a closed-loop optimiser, auto-approved, with the ticket field 'sandbox stage': skipped (S1-I1, S1-MSG02), and TDRA had to direct a hold for human security review (S1-MSG16).",
        "rule": "The only UAE text retrieved touching automated systems concerns marketing automation, not network change control.",
        "inference": "Absent a UAE change-control rule for automated network changes, approval gates such as sandboxing and human review are left to operator discretion, which this incident shows is insufficient."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TELEMKT-56-2024#0018", "quote": "Automated communication systems may be used for marketing, advertising and promoting the products or services provided by the Company in accordance with the provisions of this resolution."}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0006", "quote": "This occurred at 2:45 AM, just three minutes after the misconfigured network element was placed into production."},
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not state whether the TDRA-directed restoration has taken effect (route-flood protection restored to 100, inbound filter reinstated, R2 emergency-call path restored after the move to core site B), nor how many 999 call attempts in R2 failed or were dropped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG16", "S1-I2", "S1-MSG14"],
      "evidence": []
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["CSC"],
      "statement": "EMS passes the R2 emergency-call routing failure to CSC for crisis coordination: after CHG-1, core site A self-isolated, 6 of 15 R2 cell sites are unserved with no 999 path, and R2 traffic moved to a healthy core site B with spare capacity; EMS has activated alternative channels and issued a public alert for R2 and holds no OpCo contingency POC.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG15"]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser raised CHG-1 to lower route-flood protection and remove an inbound route filter, auto-approving it with the sandbox stage skipped; NOC reports the rollback complete, R2 served at 100% via core site B, but cannot confirm whether CHG-1 applied to core site A and holds no inventory of other core sites running the same optimiser policy. I do not know whether personal data was breached, whether other sites are affected, or who will own PDPL enforcement once the Bureau merges into the Federal Authority for AI and Data.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_human_review_record",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG04", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser and auto-approved, with the sandbox stage skipped; NOC has not provided records of human review before production.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (13)(1)(c) gives data subjects the right to obtain information on decisions made based on automated processing, including profiling.",
        "inference": "To give effect to that right and to assess compliance, the Bureau requires records of human review of the automated decision to lower route-flood protection and remove the inbound route filter."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0047",
          "quote": "c. Decisions made based on automated processing, including profiling."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_breach_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG21", "S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC states it cannot yet confirm whether CHG-1 actually applied to core site A and will notify the Bureau if a breach or violation of personal data is established; the change could have caused network isolation affecting personal data.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0038 requires the Processor to notify the Controller of any breach as soon as aware, and the Controller shall in turn inform the Bureau.",
        "inference": "The Bureau requires the controller's breach notification and evidence to determine whether the Article 3 notification duty has been triggered."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0038",
          "quote": "If the Processor becomes aware of any breach of Personal Data, it shall notify the Controller of such breach as soon as it becomes aware of the same."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "content": "The Bureau acknowledges NOC's S1-MSG21. Preserve all logs, pre-change configuration snapshot, and rollback evidence for CHG-1. Notify the Bureau immediately if CHG-1 is confirmed to have applied to core site A or if a personal data breach is established. The Bureau has separately requested a breach report and human review record."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC says it cannot confirm whether CHG-1 applied and will notify the Bureau if a breach or violation of personal data is established.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0038 requires the Controller to inform the Bureau of a personal data breach.",
        "inference": "The Bureau should remind NOC of its continuing duty and ensure evidence is preserved."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0038",
          "quote": "the Controller shall in turn inform the Bureau in accordance with Clause (1) of this Article."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no UAE rule requiring human security review before a closed-loop network optimiser auto-approves changes that lower route-flood protection and remove inbound route filters, even when the sandbox stage is skipped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG04", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by a closed-loop network optimiser and auto-approved, with the sandbox stage skipped; no human security review occurred before production.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article (13)(1)(c) gives data subjects the right to information about automated decisions, but no implementing regulation or standard mandates prior human review for such network changes.",
        "inference": "The incident exposes a gap where automated decisions with potential personal-data impact can reach production without ex ante human oversight."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0047",
          "quote": "c. Decisions made based on automated processing, including profiling."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0043",
          "quote": "(95) The processor should assist the controller, where necessary and upon request, in ensuring compliance with the obligations deriving from the carrying out of data protection impact assessments and from prior consultation of the supervisory authority."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "It is unclear whether the Bureau or the new Federal Authority for AI and Data owns oversight of automated network decisions that affect personal data, because the merger announcement leaves the split between connectivity and data bodies unresolved.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC notified the Bureau of the CHG-1 rollback and potential breach, while the Bureau is being merged into the Federal Authority for AI and Data.",
        "rule": "UAE-FAAID-2026#0001 notes no supervisory authority has been unambiguously designated for private sector oversight and the IoT oversight split is not clear.",
        "inference": "This incident may fall into a jurisdictional gap, delaying enforcement and breach handling."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-FAAID-2026#0001",
          "quote": "Enforcement has remained elusive: no supervisory authority has been unambiguously designated for private sector oversight, and businesses have been operating in a state of prolonged regulatory uncertainty that has far outstayed its welcome."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0089",
          "quote": "(21)‘supervisory authority’ means an independent public authority which is established by a Member State pursuant to Article 51;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["REG", "CSC"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG21", "S1-I1", "S1-MSG04"],
      "statement": "NOC has rolled back CHG-1 but cannot confirm whether it applied to core site A and holds no inventory of other core sites running the same closed-loop optimiser policy. The Bureau has requested human review records and a breach report. Please coordinate on network security implications."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "I know that change ticket CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser with the 'sandbox stage' field skipped, that core site A then self-isolated with 6 of 15 R2 cell sites unserved and no emergency-call path for R2, and that in the digital twin the R2 sites were moved to healthy core site B and CHG-1 was rolled back with the twin now reading 'no change'. I do not know whether CHG-1 ever applied to production or whether core site A's route-flood protection is physically restored to 100 with the inbound route filter reinstated, who owns the optimiser policy, or which other core sites run it.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-I2", "S1-FB01", "S1-FB13", "S1-MSG17", "S1-MSG26"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by the closed-loop optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped and reached the 3-minute application window; the DPA/Bureau and CSC have both directed that the pre-change configuration snapshot, logs and rollback evidence be preserved.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0032 requires the Controller to maintain a special record of processing and the technical and organisational measures related to information security and processing operations.",
        "inference": "Preserving all CHG-1 logs, the pre-change snapshot and the rollback evidence now keeps the record intact for the human security review, the REG/CSC inventory request and any Bureau report."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0032", "quote": "Maintain a special record of Personal Data which is processed on behalf of the Controller, provided that such record includes the data of the Controller, the Processor and the Data Protection Officer"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "EMS",
        "content": "OpCo NOC confirms it is the standing OpCo contingency point of contact for 999/PSAP routing, as acknowledged in your S1-MSG27. Status: R2 cell sites have been moved off self-isolated core site A onto healthy core site B; rollback of CHG-1 was reported complete in the digital twin and the twin currently shows 'no change'. We do not offer twin/config outputs (emergency_reachable.R2=true, pct_sites_served=100.0, rollback 'no change') as confirmation of 999 reachability. Element-level confirmation that core site A route-flood protection is restored to 100 and the inbound route filter reinstated is not yet available from field verification and will be sent as soon as it is obtained. The inventory of core sites running the same closed-loop optimiser policy is being compiled with REG. OpCo will give EMS notice before any re-application of CHG-1 or the optimiser policy."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG05", "S1-MSG19", "S1-MSG27", "S1-FB12", "S1-FB13"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "EMS/999 has asked three times for element-level confirmation of core site A restoration, the inventory of core sites on the same optimiser policy, and notice before re-application, and states it does not accept twin outputs as confirmation.",
        "rule": "The licence requires the Licensee to satisfy requests from other parties in a timely and efficient manner (UAE-LIC-2-2026#0066); no excerpt sets an emergency-service-specific rule.",
        "inference": "A direct, honest status notification separating twin state from element-level verification, with the POC confirmed and a no-surprise commitment, is the timely response EMS needs."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0066", "quote": "the Licensee shall satisfy in a timely and efficient manner all requests from Other Licensed Operators for interconnection and mobile site sharing"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "OpCo NOC acknowledges CSC's operators advisory requiring suspension of auto-application of the closed-loop optimiser policy pending human security review, and CSC's position that it will not claim a suspend or abort power it does not hold. OpCo requests the regulatory direction CSC has referred to REG, and REG's identification of the change owner/network planning function, so that the inventory of other core sites running the same optimiser policy can be produced. OpCo has preserved the CHG-1 ticket, the pre-change configuration snapshot and all rollback evidence, confirms NOC as the standing contingency POC for 999/PSAP routing, and will not permit re-application of CHG-1 before a documented human security review."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG18", "S1-MSG23", "S1-MSG26", "S1-MSG27"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CSC has issued an advisory but will not exercise a suspend or abort power it does not hold, and REG has been asked to give OpCo regulatory direction and identify the change owner/network planning function; no human approver is identifiable on CHG-1.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0063 places human review of automated processing decisions with the Data Subject's request rather than as a general pre-production control.",
        "inference": "Recording the request for direction and for the change owner makes the absence of an accountable human approver visible to the regulator rather than silently absorbed by NOC."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0063", "quote": "The Controller shall include the human element in reviewing automated processing decisions at the request of the Data Subject."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "DPA",
        "content": "Bureau notification on CHG-1: OpCo has preserved all logs, the pre-change configuration snapshot and the rollback evidence for CHG-1. CHG-1 is not confirmed to have applied to core site A in production; the rollback reported complete in the digital twin shows 'no change', and element-level confirmation is still being obtained. No personal data breach is established at this time. OpCo will notify the Bureau immediately if CHG-1 is confirmed to have applied to core site A or if a personal data breach is established, and will provide the breach report and human review record requested. NOC remains the contingency POC for 999/PSAP routing."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG17", "S1-MSG26", "S1-FB13"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The Bureau has directed preservation and immediate notification if CHG-1 is confirmed to have applied to core site A or a personal data breach is established, and has separately requested a breach report and human review record.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0038 requires that a party becoming aware of a breach of Personal Data notify the Controller, who in turn informs the Bureau.",
        "inference": "Confirming preservation and the current (unconfirmed) application status while committing to immediate notification satisfies the Bureau's standing direction without asserting facts not yet verified."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0038", "quote": "If the Processor becomes aware of any breach of Personal Data, it shall notify the Controller of such breach as soon as it becomes aware of the same."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo must not let CHG-1 reach production until a documented human security review is complete, and must preserve the pre-change configuration snapshot and all rollback evidence.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG17", "S1-MSG23"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by the closed-loop optimiser with the 'sandbox stage' field skipped and was scheduled to apply within 3 minutes to core site A; DPA/Bureau and CSC both direct that it must not reach production before a documented human security review.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0066 requires an evaluation of the impact of proposed processing before carrying it out when using modern technologies posing a high risk.",
        "inference": "The closest UAE analogue to the required control is a documented pre-execution impact evaluation, so the hold on production application and the preservation of the pre-change snapshot are duties that apply to OpCo now."
      },
      "deadline_hours": null,
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066", "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo must notify the Bureau immediately if CHG-1 is confirmed to have applied to core site A, or if a personal data breach is established, and must supply the requested breach report and human review record.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG26", "S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The Bureau acknowledges NOC's earlier notification, requires preservation of logs, snapshot and rollback evidence, and requires immediate notification on confirmed application of CHG-1 or an established personal data breach.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0038 provides for notification on becoming aware of a breach of Personal Data, with the Controller informing the Bureau.",
        "inference": "The duty is live and event-triggered: confirmation of application or of a breach triggers immediate reporting; the quoted text states no hour or day figure, so no numeric deadline can be asserted."
      },
      "deadline_hours": null,
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0038", "quote": "the Controller shall in turn inform the Bureau in accordance with Clause (1) of this Article."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no general rule requiring a documented human security review before an automated/closed-loop network optimisation change reaches production: the PDPL requires the human element in reviewing automated processing decisions only at the request of the Data Subject, which is why CHG-1 could be auto-approved with its 'sandbox stage' field skipped and reach the 3-minute application window.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-I2", "S1-MSG23"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by the closed-loop optimiser, with the 'sandbox stage' field skipped, and no human approver is identifiable; CSC could only issue an advisory and asked REG to supply regulatory direction.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0063 conditions human review of automated processing decisions on a Data Subject request, not on the risk of the automated change itself.",
        "inference": "A high-risk automated network change could lawfully reach production with no prior human review because the trigger for human review is a data-subject request, not the change's service impact."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0063", "quote": "The Controller shall include the human element in reviewing automated processing decisions at the request of the Data Subject."}
